{
  "dom_id": "step-q110207",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The first term of a geometric sequence is $\\frac{1}{4}$ and the common ratio is $4.$ Written in sigma notation, what is the sum of the first $50$ terms?",
  "worked_solution": "First, we must express the series in the form:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{N}{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ denotes the first term of the series, $r$ denotes the common ratio, and $N$ denotes the number of terms in the series. In this case, ${a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4},$ $r=4$ and $N=50.$\n\nExpressing the geometric series in sigma notation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n{S}_{50}={\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {4}^{n-1}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nFinally, we can simplify the above using the laws of exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {4}^{n-1} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}{4}^{-1}\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}{4}^{n-1-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{50}{4}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
